# Architecture

## 1. Overview

The solution uses Nginx as the entry point for client traffic, routing requests to separate backend applications based on the requested URL path.

The initial implementation consists of three services:

- Nginx: Reverse proxy and central entry point.
- Node.js: Web application serving the homepage.
- Python FastAPI: Backend API service.

The services run as separate Docker containers and communicate over a private Docker network.

Only Nginx publishes ports to the host. The backend applications are not directly exposed.

